for (const [initializerIdentifier, componentIdentifiers] of Object.entries(jsComponentInitializers)) {
  const initializerFunc = DotNet.findJSFunction(initializerIdentifier, 0) as JSComponentInitializerCallback;
  for (const componentIdentifier of componentIdentifiers)
    initializerFunc(componentIdentifier, jsComponentParameters[componentIdentifier]);
}

if (manager && currentRendererId === rendererId) {
    // A different renderer type (e.g., Server vs WebAssembly) is trying to enable JS root components.
    // This is a multi-host scenario which is not supported for dynamic root components.
    throw new Error('Dynamic root components have already been enabled.');
  }

// When the same renderer type re-enables (e.g., circuit restart or new circuit on same page),
  // accept the new manager. The old manager's DotNetObjectReference is no longer valid anyway
  // because the old circuit is gone. We don't dispose the old manager - doing so would cause
  // JSDisconnectedException because the circuit that created it no longer exists.
  currentRendererId = rendererId;
  manager = managerInstance;

[Theory]
[InlineData("ServerNonPrerendered")]
[InlineData("WebAssemblyNonPrerendered")]
public void PersistentStateIsSupportedInDynamicJSRoots(string renderMode)
{
    Navigate($"subdir/WasmMinimal/dynamic-js-root.html?renderMode={renderMode}");

    Browser.Equal("Counter", () => Browser.Exists(By.TagName("h1")).Text);
    Browser.Equal("Current count: 0", () => Browser.Exists(By.CssSelector("p[role='status']")).Text);

    Browser.Click(By.CssSelector("button.btn-primary"));
    Browser.Equal("Current count: 1", () => Browser.Exists(By.CssSelector("p[role='status']")).Text);
}

findings.body:
The guard at line 126 throws when `currentRendererId === rendererId`. That is the restart case the PR is meant to allow: a new Server circuit reuses rendererId 0, so `enableJSRootComponents` throws 'Dynamic root components have already been enabled.' on every restart. Meanwhile a WebAssembly host with a different rendererId (1) passes the check and silently overwrites `manager`, the opposite of the behavior the comment and PR description specify.

::diff{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="126-130"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The comment on lines 127-128 and the PR description both say a different renderer must throw. The condition needs to be `!==`, not `===`.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="126-126"}
if (manager && currentRendererId !== rendererId) {

The diff removes `jsComponentParametersByIdentifier = jsComponentParameters;` from `enableJSRootComponents`, and nothing else in the head assigns it. `RootComponentsFunctions.add` reads `jsComponentParametersByIdentifier[componentIdentifier]` at line 30 on every call, so it throws a TypeError ('Cannot read properties of undefined') even on the first circuit. The page never renders the component, which breaks the feature the test `PersistentStateIsSupportedInDynamicJSRoots` depends on.

::diff{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="134-137"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The restart path also needs the map refreshed. On a new circuit the metadata may be the new one, so the map should be replaced along with `manager` and not left pointing at the first circuit's value.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="137-137"}
  manager = managerInstance;
  jsComponentParametersByIdentifier = jsComponentParameters;

The only test added is `PersistentStateIsSupportedInDynamicJSRoots`, which loads the page once and checks the counter. That covers first-circuit rendering, which is the path that was already working before this PR (and which the missing assignment currently breaks). Nothing covers the two behaviors the PR changes: a second circuit on the same page enabling without error, and a second, different-renderer host throwing. Either of those tests would have caught the inverted guard.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/Tests/StatePersistenceTest.cs" lines="279-291"}

::callout{type="info"}
A JS-side unit test around `enableJSRootComponents` with a stubbed `DotNet.DotNetObject` would be cheap and would cover both guard branches. The E2E test should also reload or restart the circuit once, so the restart path runs in the browser.

The conditional `--RegisterDynamicJSRootComponent` flag is removed, so `dynamic-js-root-counter` is always registered for every app built on `RazorComponentEndpointsStartup`. Any of those apps now runs `enableJSRootComponents` on render, and the manager is created for every circuit even when no test uses the dynamic root. The PR's stated goal is to undo the extra test architecture from #64159, so an unconditional registration goes against that. The flag and the Program.cs entry were removed together, which is consistent, but the wider effect on the shared test host is not explained anywhere.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/testassets/Components.TestServer/RazorComponentEndpointsStartup.cs" lines="54-54"}

::callout{type="info"}
If the test really needs this registration only on the dynamic-root page, consider keeping the flag and passing it through the fixture's AdditionalArguments as the original test did. If unconditional registration is intended, call that out in the PR description.
